# harness|signal|slot|priority
#
# signal    gpu:pattern      a program REALLY holding a card — the safest
#           process:pattern  a command line (fragile: see below)
#           port:number      an ESTABLISHED connection, not a mere listener
# priority  highest wins; a game comes first, because a stutter is visible
#           and a background job waiting twenty seconds is not
#
# WHY `gpu:` IS THE SAFE ONE. Matching command lines bites twice: kernel
# threads carry their name in brackets, so `reaper` matches [oom_reaper] and
# your game looks permanently active; and any command that merely MENTIONS
# the pattern triggers it, including the watcher's own. A program holding
# card memory is a fact, not a string.

game|gpu:.exe,steam|free-c0|100
studio|gpu:comfy,diffusion|free-all|80
chat|port:10369|assistant-c1|50
